# =============================================================================
# CareerDossierTeX keeps source text in Git. Generated documents, LaTeX build
# artifacts, local configuration, private data, and third-party binaries belong
# outside the repository.
# =============================================================================

# --- LaTeX build artifacts ---
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.dvi
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.lof
*.lot
*.nav
*.out
*.run.xml
*.snm
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.vrb
*.xdv

# --- Generated documents and archives ---
*.pdf
*.doc
*.docx
*.key
*.numbers
*.odt
*.pages
*.ppt
*.pptx
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# --- Generated images and media ---
*.gif
*.heic
*.HEIC
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.mov
*.mp4
*.png
*.webp

# CONTRIBUTING.md permits reviewed preview PNGs under docs/assets/.
!docs/assets/
!docs/assets/**/*.png

# --- Third-party font binaries ---
*.otf
*.ttf
*.woff
*.woff2

# --- Secrets, local preferences, and private personal data ---
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
# Agent worktrees. Claude Code's own worktree isolation checks a branch out
# under .claude/worktrees/<name>/, which git reports as an untracked directory
# in the parent checkout. The tooling writes the same pattern into
# .git/info/exclude, but that file is per-clone and is never committed, so
# without this line a fresh clone or a second machine surfaces the directory
# again. The contents are a checkout, not source: the branch is the artifact
# worth keeping, and the worktree is removed when the session ends.
.claude/worktrees/
.env
*.local
secrets/
**/private/
referees_private.csv
recommendation_letters/

# --- Operating-system and editor files ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- test artifacts ---
# Compiled PDFs, logs, aux, and out files are already ignored globally above;
# these cover the remaining per-runner scratch files under tests/.
*.stdout
# Every runner writes *.diff scratch files next to its fixtures, not just the
# extraction one.
tests/*/*.diff
# tests/links/run.sh extracts each fixture's `% LINKTOKEN:` directives into a
# companion *.tokens file for the checker to read. The directives are the
# source; the extracted file is scratch.
tests/*/*.tokens
# tests/bibliography/run.sh captures the guard's diagnosis for its negative
# control in a *.guard file so the runner can report it after deciding the
# verdict. Generated evidence, like the two above.
tests/*/*.guard
# The extraction and bibliography runners write the text they extracted to a
# *.got file and diff that against the committed baseline, rather than diffing
# against a process substitution the sandbox denies (issue #392). The baseline
# is source; what a run happened to extract is scratch.
tests/*/*.got

# veraPDF reports and the toolchain record from tests/tagging/run.sh. These are
# evidence retained as CI artifacts and reviewed per run, not committed files.
tests/tagging/reports/

# l3build writes its check sandbox and diffs here; the .tlg baselines under
# tests/regression/ are source and are not ignored.
/build/
